# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Ablation caches are NOT IGNORED — they are trackable, and right now there are
# NONE. See KNOWN_ISSUES.md 0z23.
#
# They were tracked from 2026-09-05 so a clone could reproduce or extend the
# tables without the run. The cost is that a stale cache arrives with a
# checkout, so docs/ABLATION_CACHES.md records a source fingerprint per deck and
# you check it before resuming one. That safety net was then not maintained: ten
# caches were deleted in b09055c without the generator being re-run, leaving the
# manifest describing fourteen files of which four existed — and all four of
# those disagreed with their live fingerprint. They were deleted on 2026-09-16
# and results/caches/ is empty.
#
# The argument for tracking them had already weakened on its own terms: the
# "roughly six hours to rebuild" that justified it is now about 23 minutes.
# If you produce a cache worth keeping, commit it together with its NOTES entry
# and a regenerated manifest — an untracked cache with no provenance is the
# thing this comment exists to prevent.
#
# The blank mode is IN THE FILENAME on purpose: a cache measured against a
# different blank is not resumable onto, and a suffix nothing reads is how the
# N-in-the-key bug happened the first time.

# Spreadsheet lock/temp files
~$*.xlsx
.~lock.*

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Everything below moved under results/ in the 2026-09-09 reorganisation. The
# patterns are anchored there rather than left bare, so a stray ablation_*.log
# written into the root by a script run the wrong way is VISIBLE in git status
# instead of silently ignored.

# Ablation stderr progress logs — noise, the .txt tables are the artefact
results/ablation_*.log

# Regeneration scratch — the finished .txt tables ARE tracked
results/ablation_*.txt.new
results/regen.log

# A void table kept only long enough to diff against; not an artefact.
results/ablation_*_VOID_*.txt

# tutor_policy.py's scratch log
results/tutor_log.json

# check_unchanged_decks.py's baseline dumps
results/baselines*.json
